2025-05-20T03:59:10Z","updated_at":"2025-06-24T23:43:27Z","closed_at":"2025-06-24T23:43:27Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nhas issue: \n- 4.5dev4, macOS 15.1\n\nworks:\n- 4.5dev4, windows11\n- 4.4.1 windows11\n- 4.4.1 macOS 15.1\n\n### System information\n\nMacOS Sequoia 15.1 (24B2082)\n\n### Issue description\n\nOn the 4.5dev4 inputs from the Xbox controller are sent twice.\n\nThis is the input code:\n\n```gdscript\nfunc _unhandled_input(event: InputEvent) -> void:\n\t# Hide/show the main menu\n\tif event.is_action_released(\"ui_menu\", true):\n\t\tvisibile = not visible\n```\n\nI have a standard xbox controller plugged in via USBC.\n\nWhen I run the same project with 4.4.1, controller inputs are registered correctly.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nIn the sample project...\n \n- Attach an xbox controller via USBC\n- Launch the project in 4.5dev4 on osx\n- Press the xbox \"menu\" button\n\nExpected:\n- gray circle toggles visibility\n\nResults:\n- gray circle briefly flashes between visible/not visible and then back to visible.\n\nImpact:\n- Controllers on MacOS are likely broken and unusable.\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[godot-input-bug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20323209/godot-input-bug.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_